          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "The maximum value of $z=6 x+8 y$ subject to constraints $2 x+y \\leq 30, x+2 y \\leq 24$ and $x \\geq 0, y \\geq 0$ is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "JsWko",
              "text": "90",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "g1woE",
              "text": "120",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "gFa99",
              "text": "96",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "XCbTI",
              "text": "240",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Here, $2 x+y \\leq 30, x+2 y \\leq 24, x, y \\geq 0$\r\n\r\nThe shaded region represents the feasible region, hence $\\mathrm{z}=6 \\mathrm{x}+8 \\mathrm{y}$. Obviously it is maximum at (12,6) Hence $z=12 \\times 6+8 \\times 6=120$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/qxz5bvmr2xmJCHqxpyt9F0AeSB9p03OvCuJniSYliOI.original.fullsize.png\">",
            "image": null
          },
