          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "The maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></math> subject to constraints <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "W9MRI",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "ZuUpN",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "azm7q",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "MCLtb",
              "text": "None of these",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "We have,<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></math></p><p>And,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Let</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Then the feasible region is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/3697c4e7-aefa-40a0-89bf-3ff4d8185590-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 238px;\" /></p><p>From the figure, it is clear that there is no common area. So, we cannot find maximum value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence, option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>d</mi></mfenced></math> is correct.</p>",
            "image": null
          },
